{
  "uid": "homelab-site-service-health",
  "title": "Site & Service Health \u2014 Home / Oracle / Canada",
  "description": "Which site is each service at, and is it up. Every service row carries an explicit Site column. HOME is this k3s cluster and is fully instrumented; Kubernetes objects have no site label of their own, so this dashboard stamps site=\"home\" onto them with label_replace \u2014 a definition, not a measurement. ORACLE runs a separate, non-federated Prometheus and CANADA has no scrape target at all, so both are reported as \"unknown from here\" rather than faked. Both of those panels count targets instead of probing a hard-coded job name, so they start working by themselves once the corresponding scrape job is added. Rebuilt 2026-09-21: the previous Canada panel queried up{job=\"canada-pantry-bot-api\"}, a job present in neither the repo nor the live Prometheus config, so it could only ever render No data.",
  "tags": [
    "homelab",
    "sites",
    "failover",
    "health",
    "pantry-bot"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": true,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 2,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "links": [
    {
      "title": "Per-service dashboards",
      "type": "dashboards",
      "tags": [
        "service"
      ],
      "asDropdown": true,
      "icon": "external link",
      "includeVars": false,
      "keepTime": true,
      "targetBlank": false,
      "tooltip": "",
      "url": ""
    }
  ],
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "DS_PROMETHEUS",
        "label": "Prometheus",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0,
        "refresh": 1,
        "regex": "",
        "skipUrlSync": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Site map \u2014 which site is each service at?",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Every service row below carries an explicit **Site** column, so no panel here requires you to already know where something runs.\n\n| Site | What it is | How this Prometheus sees it |\n|---|---|---|\n| **HOME** | MinecraftMachine, the single-node k3s cluster on the home LAN (192.168.40.208) | Fully instrumented: kube-state-metrics, cAdvisor, Alloy/Loki, plus per-microservice `/metrics` scrape jobs. Kubernetes objects carry no `site` label, so this dashboard stamps `site=\"home\"` onto them with `label_replace` \u2014 that is a definition, not a measurement. |\n| **ORACLE** | Oracle Cloud failover site | **Not federated into this Prometheus.** `observability/oracle-prometheus-config.yaml` configures a *separate* Prometheus at Oracle; nothing from it is remote-written or federated here, so every Oracle question is answered \"unknown from here\" rather than guessed. |\n| **CANADA** | Last-resort recovery site | **No scrape target exists.** There is no `canada-*` job in `observability/prometheus-config.yaml` and no series carries `site=\"canada\"`. The Canada panel below reports the count of configured Canada targets, so it turns green by itself the day one is added. |\n| **GREENIE'S PC** | Windows/Docker gaming PC (`ThePantry`) | Reaches this Prometheus via Alloy remote-write as `site=\"windows-remote\"`. Detail on the Greenie's Main PC dashboard. |"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "HOME \u2014 scrape targets up",
      "description": "Targets this Prometheus scrapes that belong to the home cluster.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(up{site=\"home\"} or up{job!~\".*oracle.*|canada-.*\"} unless up{site!=\"\"})",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
