      "title": "Canada has no scrape target in this Prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 57
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Canada is a Windows/Docker host outside Kubernetes. `observability/failover-witness/CANADA-METRICS-RELAY.md` describes a relay and says the Prometheus target is enabled, but **no `canada-*` job exists in `observability/prometheus-config.yaml` and no series carries `site=\"canada\"`** \u2014 the document is ahead of the config.\n\nAn earlier version of this dashboard hard-coded `up{job=\"canada-pantry-bot-api\"}`, a job name that exists in neither the repo config nor the live one, so the panel could only ever render \"No data\". The CANADA stat above counts `site=\"canada\"` targets instead, which is truthful today and self-healing later.\n\nHost telemetry for Canada would follow the pattern Greenie's PC already proves: Alloy remote-write with a `site` label."
      }
    },
